Exit Status in shell is a number that will determine whether it is successful or not.

Number ranges from 0-255
0 - Universal Success for any command
1-255 is error depends on the command
0-125 is recommended for users to use, whereas numbers from 126-255 are generally used by system.
To refer to exit status we use $? , To print exit status on screen it is echo $?
If we have pipes in command, then last command status will get printed.
cat /etc/passwd | grep root
Here grep command status will be printed.
